1
00:00:19,128 --> 00:00:21,758
I love Seok Jin.

2
00:00:22,158 --> 00:00:23,528
Hello, Seok Jin.

3
00:00:24,328 --> 00:00:27,598
(My Star and Star Lee)

4
00:00:28,168 --> 00:00:29,767
(Today's My Star...)

5
00:00:29,768 --> 00:00:33,638
(makes Seo Jin, the non-emotional type, cry.)

6
00:00:34,138 --> 00:00:38,847
(He even touches his heart.)

7
00:00:38,848 --> 00:00:42,178
(Another older bestie of Seo Jin's makes an appearance.)

8
00:00:42,848 --> 00:00:44,518
He's 60.

9
00:00:44,888 --> 00:00:46,788
And he does things like this.

10
00:00:47,758 --> 00:00:49,787
You should stir your milkshake well.

11
00:00:49,788 --> 00:00:50,908
(Seo Jin's new older bestie)

12
00:00:51,328 --> 00:00:52,757
I used to do this.

13
00:00:52,758 --> 00:00:53,828
(Next to him is...)

14
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:57,827
(The winner of the Excellence Award in the Female Category...)

15
00:00:57,828 --> 00:01:00,068
(at the 2025 SBS Entertainment Awards)

16
00:01:00,698 --> 00:01:03,798
(She cried while delivering an acceptance speech.)

17
00:01:04,338 --> 00:01:06,438
(Laughing)

18
00:01:08,108 --> 00:01:09,478
She's hilarious, isn't she?

19
00:01:10,208 --> 00:01:12,148
(She made Seo Jin laugh.)

20
00:01:12,578 --> 00:01:15,878
(What do the two people Seo Jin likes have in common?)

21
00:01:16,978 --> 00:01:18,947
(They formed a band...)

22
00:01:18,948 --> 00:01:20,288
(called CHOONGJU JI-C.)

23
00:01:20,948 --> 00:01:24,018
(They even released a song together.)

24
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:26,527
(Ji Ye Eun and Jee Seok Jin from CHOONGJU JI-C)

25
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:27,757
- It's so funny.
- Milkshake

26
00:01:27,758 --> 00:01:30,928
(My Star is waiting for the secretaries.)

27
00:01:32,168 --> 00:01:33,228
Seo Jin is here.

28
00:01:33,868 --> 00:01:34,897
Should we welcome them?

29
00:01:34,898 --> 00:01:36,338
Why is it different from the usual?

30
00:01:36,698 --> 00:01:39,014
- Are they supposed to come?
- Why should we welcome them?

31
00:01:39,038 --> 00:01:41,014
- Do we need to go over to his car?
- Where is his car?

32
00:01:41,038 --> 00:01:43,077
So we have to welcome him today.

33
00:01:43,078 --> 00:01:44,377
Hello.

34
00:01:44,378 --> 00:01:45,507
Please get out.

35
00:01:45,508 --> 00:01:47,477
- Hello.
- Come on.

36
00:01:47,478 --> 00:01:48,517
(He's flustered for real.)

37
00:01:48,518 --> 00:01:49,518
Why...

38
00:01:49,718 --> 00:01:50,877
Why do you always look so cool?

39
00:01:50,878 --> 00:01:52,148
I like your outfit.

40
00:01:52,988 --> 00:01:54,017
Hello.

41
00:01:54,018 --> 00:01:55,988
- I like your necklace too.
- Your necklace.

42
00:01:57,288 --> 00:01:59,127
- You guys haven't met before.
- Right.

43
00:01:59,128 --> 00:02:00,428
We haven't met before, right?

44
00:02:01,658 --> 00:02:02,757
- You're very tall.
- Yes.

45
00:02:02,758 --> 00:02:04,227
- She's taller than you think.
- I'm taller than I look.

46
00:02:04,228 --> 00:02:05,327
She's 170cm.

47
00:02:05,328 --> 00:02:06,968
- I'm 171cm. Yes.
- Are you 171cm?

48
00:02:07,328 --> 00:02:09,137
Is she the most beautiful Ji?

49
00:02:09,138 --> 00:02:11,207
- Totally. She's the best.
- Is that so?

50
00:02:11,208 --> 00:02:12,737
(His compliments level up every week.)

51
00:02:12,738 --> 00:02:13,907
(She's loving it.)

52
00:02:13,908 --> 00:02:15,107
She was nervous because you guys...

53
00:02:15,108 --> 00:02:16,277
- haven't met before.
- I was.

54
00:02:16,278 --> 00:02:17,654
- There's no need to be nervous.
- Yes.

55
00:02:17,678 --> 00:02:18,848
Why don't we have a seat?

56
00:02:18,978 --> 00:02:21,318
Let's have a seat.

57
00:02:22,118 --> 00:02:23,148
Gosh.

58
00:02:23,618 --> 00:02:25,048
(Staring)

59
00:02:25,288 --> 00:02:26,448
Now...

60
00:02:26,988 --> 00:02:28,257
it's cold enough to wear...

61
00:02:28,258 --> 00:02:30,387
- a lightweight puffer jacket.
- I know.

62
00:02:30,388 --> 00:02:32,288
(It's that time of year.)

63
00:02:32,388 --> 00:02:33,857
It's cute.

64
00:02:33,858 --> 00:02:36,298
(His older bestie is after his clothes, just like Kwang Kyu.)

65
00:02:36,898 --> 00:02:38,397
It suddenly got chilly.

66
00:02:38,398 --> 00:02:39,467
(A puffer jacket perfect for the fall)

67
00:02:39,468 --> 00:02:40,468
Have a seat here.

68
00:02:40,628 --> 00:02:42,168
I call him Star Lee.

69
00:02:42,768 --> 00:02:44,214
- Star Lee.
- What are you talking about?

70
00:02:44,238 --> 00:02:45,667
(The thing Star Lee is most curious about right now)

71
00:02:45,668 --> 00:02:46,838
So...

72
00:02:47,008 --> 00:02:48,177
I heard you're getting married.

73
00:02:48,178 --> 00:02:49,418
- Yes.
- She's getting married.

74
00:02:49,478 --> 00:02:51,677
(Ye Eun will get married in the winter.)

75
00:02:51,678 --> 00:02:52,847
(Vata)

76
00:02:52,848 --> 00:02:55,978
(Dancer Vata choreographed a dance for CHOONGJU JI-C.)

77
00:02:56,118 --> 00:02:57,847
("Ji Ye Eun and Vata to Tie the Knot After 5 Months of Public Dating")

78
00:02:57,848 --> 00:02:59,808
("Ji Ye Eun and Vata to Get Married in December")

79
00:03:00,788 --> 00:03:01,858
In December?

80
00:03:02,158 --> 00:03:03,158
Why are you getting married so soon?

81
00:03:03,158 --> 00:03:04,158
- Why don't you take your time?
- I just...

82
00:03:04,159 --> 00:03:06,087
- I know. That's what I told her.
- Right?

83
00:03:06,088 --> 00:03:07,587
- I mean...
- You know how bad it can be.

84
00:03:07,588 --> 00:03:08,627
You should stop her.

85
00:03:08,628 --> 00:03:10,927
- True.
- Why?

86
00:03:10,928 --> 00:03:12,097
- Seok Jin!
- You should stop her.

87
00:03:12,098 --> 00:03:13,897
- You said you were happy for us.
- I mean...

88
00:03:13,898 --> 00:03:15,398
You know it best.

89
00:03:15,798 --> 00:03:17,197
You should stop her.

90
00:03:17,198 --> 00:03:18,937
- You don't have time for this.
- I mean...

91
00:03:18,938 --> 00:03:20,308
You want to live the single life.

92
00:03:21,808 --> 00:03:24,038
- Right?
- That's a ridiculous rumour.

93
00:03:24,138 --> 00:03:25,247
- No, I don't.
- You want to live the single life.

94
00:03:25,248 --> 00:03:28,047
My wife and I went on a trip recently.

95
00:03:28,048 --> 00:03:29,077
They went to Rome.

96
00:03:29,078 --> 00:03:30,348
Didn't she drag you along?

97
00:03:31,218 --> 00:03:32,248
Really?

98
00:03:33,518 --> 00:03:35,188
I always wanted to visit Rome.

99
00:03:35,418 --> 00:03:38,187
I wanted to go too. I wanted to go to Europe.

100
00:03:38,188 --> 00:03:39,758
Then why do you look so unhappy?

101
00:03:40,128 --> 00:03:41,557
- Why do you look so unhappy?
- Italy was...

102
00:03:41,558 --> 00:03:43,228
You look very pale.

103
00:03:44,898 --> 00:03:46,168
No, I'm fine.

104
00:03:46,398 --> 00:03:48,337
Imagine what I had to go through.

105
00:03:48,338 --> 00:03:50,298
- I lost 3kg.
- While travelling?

106
00:03:50,668 --> 00:03:53,237
I walked 20,000 steps a day.

107
00:03:53,238 --> 00:03:54,267
So you were stressed out.

108
00:03:54,268 --> 00:03:56,337
(He's worried about how My Star is doing.)

109
00:03:56,338 --> 00:03:58,448
Are you against marriage?

110
00:03:58,778 --> 00:04:01,448
- No, I'm not.
- You're not?

111
00:04:01,578 --> 00:04:02,854
So you just want to get married later?

112
00:04:02,878 --> 00:04:04,647
People these days have been getting married at a young age again.

113
00:04:04,648 --> 00:04:05,688
- Is that so?
- Yes.

114
00:04:06,088 --> 00:04:07,818
I went to the hairdresser today.

115
00:04:07,888 --> 00:04:09,457
So many people...

116
00:04:09,458 --> 00:04:11,194
- were going to a wedding.
- There are so many people.

117
00:04:11,218 --> 00:04:13,357
And it's nice to wear a wedding dress when you're still young.

118
00:04:13,358 --> 00:04:15,097
- Today...
- You can take...

119
00:04:15,098 --> 00:04:16,397
the wedding dress off later. No, never mind.

120
00:04:16,398 --> 00:04:18,997
(You can take the wedding dress off later.)

121
00:04:18,998 --> 00:04:20,168
- What?
- I mean...

122
00:04:20,528 --> 00:04:22,298
(Oh, no)

123
00:04:22,438 --> 00:04:23,468
- What?
- I mean...

124
00:04:24,538 --> 00:04:27,008
This boomer... He really is a boomer.

125
00:04:27,508 --> 00:04:29,638
It's because so many couples go separate ways.

126
00:04:29,778 --> 00:04:31,237
Why would you say that...

127
00:04:31,238 --> 00:04:33,808
to someone who is getting married?

128
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:35,847
(Another boomer is just having fun.)

129
00:04:35,848 --> 00:04:37,317
- When are you getting married?
- Sorry?

130
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:38,818
December.

131
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:41,087
- It's still a long way off.
- Two months are left.

132
00:04:41,088 --> 00:04:42,917
"It's still a long way off."

133
00:04:42,918 --> 00:04:44,517
- That means...
- Only two months are left.

134
00:04:44,518 --> 00:04:45,957
Does that mean it's not too late to take it back?

135
00:04:45,958 --> 00:04:47,427
You still have a lot of time.

136
00:04:47,428 --> 00:04:48,657
- So think it through.
- You still have a lot of time.

137
00:04:48,658 --> 00:04:50,858
I think...

138
00:04:51,158 --> 00:04:52,668
you've never experienced true love.

139
00:04:54,228 --> 00:04:55,338
That's what I think.

140
00:04:55,768 --> 00:04:57,037
Why don't you come to our church?

141
00:04:57,038 --> 00:04:58,337
(Come to our church to learn what true love is.)

142
00:04:58,338 --> 00:04:59,467
I've tried everything.

143
00:04:59,468 --> 00:05:01,338
- I've been to church.
- You have?

144
00:05:01,508 --> 00:05:02,937
Right. How...

145
00:05:02,938 --> 00:05:05,008
- Oh, Kwang Kyu is here.
- Is Kwang Kyu here?

146
00:05:05,608 --> 00:05:07,448
- Hello.
- I have it too.

147
00:05:07,978 --> 00:05:09,278
- Kwang Kyu.
- Seok Jin.

148
00:05:09,348 --> 00:05:10,547
- How have you been?
- Hello.

149
00:05:10,548 --> 00:05:12,017
It's nice to meet you.

150
00:05:12,018 --> 00:05:14,818
You're a celebrity. Why are you wearing a cap like that?

151
00:05:15,688 --> 00:05:18,087
- My goodness.
- I'm your manager.

152
00:05:18,088 --> 00:05:20,588
- Right. You're my secretary today.
- Yes.

153
00:05:20,788 --> 00:05:21,798
Your cap...

154
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:24,997
(A military cap, floral patterns, chequered patterns, a rock star)

155
00:05:24,998 --> 00:05:26,368
Where did you get that cap?

156
00:05:26,768 --> 00:05:28,438
It's not easy to find.

157
00:05:29,698 --> 00:05:31,667
- Are those your own clothes?
- What?

158
00:05:31,668 --> 00:05:33,107
- Are those your own clothes?
- Are these my own clothes?

159
00:05:33,108 --> 00:05:34,667
- Yes. I'm just curious.
- Do you think...

160
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,238
his stylist got these for him?

161
00:05:36,778 --> 00:05:38,407
- There's no way.
- They don't match at all.

162
00:05:38,408 --> 00:05:40,547
- These are my clothes.
- Of course.

163
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,917
Do you think his stylist got this hat?

164
00:05:41,918 --> 00:05:44,117
- Did your stylist get your outfit?
- These are my own clothes.

165
00:05:44,118 --> 00:05:45,817
- These are my own clothes too.
- Yes.

166
00:05:45,818 --> 00:05:47,287
(Both of them are wearing their own clothes.)

167
00:05:47,288 --> 00:05:48,858
We've never met before, right?

168
00:05:49,188 --> 00:05:50,717
- What? Yes, you're right.
- We've never met before, right?

169
00:05:50,718 --> 00:05:53,027
- We've never met before.
- Yes. We've never met.

170
00:05:53,028 --> 00:05:54,858
- Amazing.
- Yes.

171
00:05:55,098 --> 00:05:57,297
You guys are still single,

172
00:05:57,298 --> 00:05:59,027
- but she's getting married already.
- Yes.

173
00:05:59,028 --> 00:06:00,397
- She's getting married in December.
- I'm getting married.

174
00:06:00,398 --> 00:06:01,478
Haven't you heard about it?

175
00:06:01,698 --> 00:06:04,298
I saw the article. Is his name Taco?

176
00:06:04,668 --> 00:06:06,107
Taco?

177
00:06:06,108 --> 00:06:07,637
- Bbatta.
- Bbatta?

178
00:06:07,638 --> 00:06:08,777
- Vata.
- "Taco?"

179
00:06:08,778 --> 00:06:10,177
- Bbatta?
- Vata.

180
00:06:10,178 --> 00:06:11,547
What's "Taco?"

181
00:06:11,548 --> 00:06:12,607
(That's not his name?)

182
00:06:12,608 --> 00:06:14,817
- It's not Bbatta. He's Vata.
- Vata.

183
00:06:14,818 --> 00:06:15,818
- Vata?
- Yes.

184
00:06:15,819 --> 00:06:17,417
- It's not Bbatta.
- No.

185
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:18,687
"Taco" is just...

186
00:06:18,688 --> 00:06:20,347
These guys are funny.

187
00:06:20,348 --> 00:06:22,634
(His name is too hard for these middle-aged men to pronounce.)

188
00:06:22,658 --> 00:06:24,987
Your career has just started. You can't get married so soon.

189
00:06:24,988 --> 00:06:26,387
I told you. He's saying the same thing.

190
00:06:26,388 --> 00:06:28,297
You guys are single, so...

191
00:06:28,298 --> 00:06:29,604
(These single middle-aged men are saying the same thing.)

192
00:06:29,628 --> 00:06:30,727
- I don't think...
- She's upset.

193
00:06:30,728 --> 00:06:31,797
I can get along with single people.

194
00:06:31,798 --> 00:06:33,428
- Life is long.
- But...

195
00:06:34,228 --> 00:06:36,398
- Hello.
- You're here.

196
00:06:36,598 --> 00:06:37,797
This is my manager.

197
00:06:37,798 --> 00:06:38,908
This is for you.

198
00:06:40,208 --> 00:06:43,678
(What's My Stars' schedule today?)

199
00:06:43,978 --> 00:06:45,778
They have a gig today in Chungju,

200
00:06:46,408 --> 00:06:48,717
the ancestral home of their clan.

201
00:06:48,718 --> 00:06:50,638
(They have a fan signing event and a gig today.)

202
00:06:50,918 --> 00:06:54,748
(Chungju's biggest music festival of the year)

203
00:06:55,458 --> 00:06:57,217
(A huge stage...)

204
00:06:57,218 --> 00:07:00,287
(featuring only top-tier pros)

205
00:07:00,288 --> 00:07:03,158
(CHOONGJU JI-C is going to Chungju!)

206
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:04,727
Is that your first event together?

207
00:07:04,728 --> 00:07:05,728
- No.
- No.

208
00:07:05,729 --> 00:07:07,297
We performed at the Waterbomb Festival.

209
00:07:07,298 --> 00:07:08,967
- We've done other gigs too.
- We've done other gigs too.

210
00:07:08,968 --> 00:07:10,137
(It's their third event.)

211
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:12,937
It's only been a year since they released a song together.

212
00:07:12,938 --> 00:07:14,138
They only have two songs.

213
00:07:14,308 --> 00:07:16,337
But they're serious about what they're doing.

214
00:07:16,338 --> 00:07:18,748
- We're serious.
- We're serious about music.

215
00:07:18,848 --> 00:07:20,307
- So...
- The vocals...

216
00:07:20,308 --> 00:07:21,878
you're serious,

217
00:07:22,018 --> 00:07:23,658
but you're rehearsing at a karaoke place?

218
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:26,487
(Time: 4pm, Location: Karaoke place, Details: Rehearsal)

219
00:07:26,488 --> 00:07:27,518
I mean...

220
00:07:28,288 --> 00:07:30,588
You're rehearsing at a karaoke place.

221
00:07:30,988 --> 00:07:33,587
- The place doesn't matter.
- We're serious. It doesn't matter.

222
00:07:33,588 --> 00:07:35,157
What matters is that we're practising.

223
00:07:35,158 --> 00:07:37,027
- Our mindset is important.
- Our mindset is important.

224
00:07:37,028 --> 00:07:39,028
You're not rehearsing on stage.

225
00:07:39,168 --> 00:07:40,644
You're rehearsing at a karaoke place.

226
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,097
- We practised a lot yesterday.
- Yes.

227
00:07:42,098 --> 00:07:43,397
- We practised yesterday.
- We practised in a studio.

228
00:07:43,398 --> 00:07:44,667
At a karaoke place?

229
00:07:44,668 --> 00:07:46,367
- No. In a studio.
- A studio near Sadang Station.

230
00:07:46,368 --> 00:07:48,107
We rehearsed with the dancers.

231
00:07:48,108 --> 00:07:49,707
- Do you have dancers too?
- Yes.

232
00:07:49,708 --> 00:07:51,608
- Four dancers.
- Really?

233
00:07:53,008 --> 00:07:57,718
(My Stars have been practising seriously for today.)

234
00:07:58,318 --> 00:08:01,918
(Sacrificing his knees)

235
00:08:02,118 --> 00:08:04,688
It'd be great if you could help them with their ending pose too.

236
00:08:05,288 --> 00:08:08,928
What's your ending pose? Is it something special?

237
00:08:09,498 --> 00:08:12,698
(Acting cute at age 60)

238
00:08:13,298 --> 00:08:15,837
(His heart skips a beat.)

239
00:08:15,838 --> 00:08:18,307
We'll be able to see everything at the karaoke place.

240
00:08:18,308 --> 00:08:20,008
- Okay.
- At the karaoke place.

241
00:08:20,238 --> 00:08:21,807
You're acting cute at 60?

242
00:08:21,808 --> 00:08:22,877
(The 60-year-old is always ready for a cute ending pose.)

243
00:08:22,878 --> 00:08:24,838
He hates it when someone mentions his age.

244
00:08:25,408 --> 00:08:26,677
- He really hates it.
- Why do you keep...

245
00:08:26,678 --> 00:08:27,884
- mentioning it?
- "You look old."

246
00:08:27,908 --> 00:08:29,677
"You look your age." He hates it when someone says these phrases.

247
00:08:29,678 --> 00:08:31,247
(Phrases he hates the most: 60, You look old, You look your age.)

248
00:08:31,248 --> 00:08:34,048
Kwang Kyu, if you speak to him with honorifics,

249
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:37,418
- people might be surprised.
- Hey, he's older than me!

250
00:08:37,588 --> 00:08:40,557
Hey, he's older than me! How should I speak to him then?

251
00:08:40,558 --> 00:08:42,898
Should I speak to him informally?

252
00:08:43,298 --> 00:08:44,858
- He's older than me.
- Hey.

253
00:08:45,398 --> 00:08:47,374
Don't speak to me formally when other people can hear you.

254
00:08:47,398 --> 00:08:48,398
- Why not?
- What?

255
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:50,767
It's like Hong Gil Dong. I can't say his name properly.

256
00:08:50,768 --> 00:08:51,807
When's your birthday?

257
00:08:51,808 --> 00:08:53,207
I was born on November 7.

258
00:08:53,208 --> 00:08:55,437
You guys are almost two years apart.

259
00:08:55,438 --> 00:08:57,077
You guys are almost two years apart.

260
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:58,078
I mean...

261
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,608
Don't speak to me with honorifics at a restaurant.

262
00:09:01,718 --> 00:09:03,447
You're still older than me, so...

263
00:09:03,448 --> 00:09:06,287
- Call him Mr. Jee.
- Mr. Jee.

264
00:09:06,288 --> 00:09:07,288
This is funny.

265
00:09:07,748 --> 00:09:09,418
As for Ye Eun,

266
00:09:10,018 --> 00:09:12,157
say something like, "you're like Jiriah Carey."

267
00:09:12,158 --> 00:09:14,998
- "Jiriah Carey?"
- I thought it was a swear word.

268
00:09:15,398 --> 00:09:17,758
- Jiriah Carey.
- Jiriah Carey.

269
00:09:17,998 --> 00:09:20,067
She likes being complimented.

270
00:09:20,068 --> 00:09:21,797
- "You're good." "You look pretty."
- Yes.

271
00:09:21,798 --> 00:09:24,568
Even dolphins need a little praise to do tricks.

272
00:09:24,968 --> 00:09:26,508
- I also...
- Whales.

273
00:09:27,038 --> 00:09:29,537
She's usually like this. Her knowledge...

274
00:09:29,538 --> 00:09:30,837
- My knowledge...
- is limited.

275
00:09:30,838 --> 00:09:32,607
But I'm a college graduate.

276
00:09:32,608 --> 00:09:34,484
Yes. She graduated from Korea National University of Arts.

277
00:09:34,508 --> 00:09:38,917
Your face looks a lot smaller in real life.

278
00:09:38,918 --> 00:09:42,617
(It instantly makes Jiriah Carey happy.)

279
00:09:42,618 --> 00:09:43,817
I told you.

280
00:09:43,818 --> 00:09:45,257
- Are you wearing contacts?
- No.

281
00:09:45,258 --> 00:09:47,327
No, I don't wear contacts.

282
00:09:47,328 --> 00:09:48,727
You're not?

283
00:09:48,728 --> 00:09:50,557
Many people say I have big pupils.

284
00:09:50,558 --> 00:09:52,067
Are your eyes naturally that colour?

285
00:09:52,068 --> 00:09:53,267
(Opening her eyes wide)

286
00:09:53,268 --> 00:09:54,698
You have beautiful eyes.

287
00:09:55,668 --> 00:09:57,697
(My Dolphin Star jumps at the compliment.)

288
00:09:57,698 --> 00:10:00,068
Thank you. Oh, my gosh.

289
00:10:00,908 --> 00:10:02,137
Her pupils are...

290
00:10:02,138 --> 00:10:04,837
- Her pupils are...
- Right?

291
00:10:04,838 --> 00:10:07,148
- Her pupils are pretty. I agree.
- I think so too.

292
00:10:08,918 --> 00:10:11,047
We prepared glasses.

293
00:10:11,048 --> 00:10:12,418
Please pick a pair...

294
00:10:12,448 --> 00:10:15,057
that suits Seok Jin.

295
00:10:15,058 --> 00:10:16,918
- You want us to pick?
- Later.

296
00:10:17,718 --> 00:10:20,527
Seo Jin knows a lot about fashion.

297
00:10:20,528 --> 00:10:21,627
(Seo Jin, who knows a lot about fashion, will choose.)

298
00:10:21,628 --> 00:10:23,758
Why do you have so many glasses?

299
00:10:23,858 --> 00:10:25,827
- They're just glasses.
- They're just glasses.

300
00:10:25,828 --> 00:10:27,508
- No sunglasses.
- They don't have lenses.

301
00:10:28,228 --> 00:10:29,897
They don't have any lenses.

302
00:10:29,898 --> 00:10:31,038
They don't.

303
00:10:31,868 --> 00:10:33,068
Why are you wearing them then?

304
00:10:34,238 --> 00:10:35,937
For the same reason you're wearing that cap.

305
00:10:35,938 --> 00:10:38,477
(For the same reason you're wearing that cap.)

306
00:10:38,478 --> 00:10:41,207
(Simple and clear)

307
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:42,378
Do you get it now?

308
00:10:42,518 --> 00:10:44,618
For the same reason you're wearing that cap.

309
00:10:45,318 --> 00:10:46,387
I totally get it.

310
00:10:46,388 --> 00:10:48,388
(Some things are more beautiful when kept hidden.)

311
00:10:48,918 --> 00:10:50,788
- What are they?
- An in-ear monitor.

312
00:10:50,888 --> 00:10:52,758
- An in-ear monitor?
- Do you use that too?

313
00:10:53,188 --> 00:10:55,027
These are customized.

314
00:10:55,028 --> 00:10:57,658
They're custom-made in-ear monitors molded to fit my ears.

315
00:10:57,898 --> 00:10:59,898
Don't you have one of these, Ye Eun?

316
00:11:00,168 --> 00:11:02,198
Why do you even need them?

317
00:11:02,298 --> 00:11:05,268
When we sing, 70 percent of the vocals are on a backing track.

318
00:11:06,068 --> 00:11:07,707
I don't know why he even uses in-ear monitors.

319
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:08,907
- A backing track?
- Yes.

320
00:11:08,908 --> 00:11:09,984
(I'm sure he doesn't need in-ear monitors.)

321
00:11:10,008 --> 00:11:11,178
You're right.

322
00:11:11,438 --> 00:11:13,607
- That's...
- Ye Eun doesn't have many lines.

323
00:11:13,608 --> 00:11:15,147
We have a backing track.

324
00:11:15,148 --> 00:11:16,677
All you do is shout "Aqua."

325
00:11:16,678 --> 00:11:18,917
"Aqua, aqua, here we go!" I do something like this.

326
00:11:18,918 --> 00:11:19,947
That's all?

327
00:11:19,948 --> 00:11:22,787
(That's all?)

328
00:11:22,788 --> 00:11:25,128
- She shouts, "Gosh, it's summer!"
- Something like that.

329
00:11:25,228 --> 00:11:27,328
"What do you want?" "Behave yourself."

330
00:11:27,388 --> 00:11:28,957
"Behave yourself and just bring a swim ring."

331
00:11:28,958 --> 00:11:30,858
Do you know why she says, "Behave yourself?"

332
00:11:31,398 --> 00:11:32,667
- That's her catchphrase.
- Yes.

333
00:11:32,668 --> 00:11:34,028
Have you heard of it?

334
00:11:34,768 --> 00:11:35,838
How do you say that?

335
00:11:36,498 --> 00:11:40,268
- "Behave yourself?"
- "Behave yourself!" Like this.

336
00:11:44,338 --> 00:11:47,207
- That's your catchphrase.
- Yes.

337
00:11:47,208 --> 00:11:49,048
- Right.
- Is there anything else?

338
00:11:50,118 --> 00:11:51,278
Shut your mouth!

339
00:11:53,388 --> 00:11:55,117
(Puzzled)

340
00:11:55,118 --> 00:11:56,687
- "Shut your mouth."
- What's that?

341
00:11:56,688 --> 00:11:59,728
- She'll say it a few times today.
- "Shut your mouth."

342
00:12:00,528 --> 00:12:04,257
No, I have a lot of respect for my elders.

343
00:12:04,258 --> 00:12:05,767
(How long will she keep respecting her elders?)

344
00:12:05,768 --> 00:12:07,297
(Worried)

345
00:12:07,298 --> 00:12:09,298
- Really?
- There's something you need to do.

346
00:12:09,968 --> 00:12:12,507
There's something you need to do. Or Star Lee could do it.

347
00:12:12,508 --> 00:12:13,607
- What is it?
- One of you two needs to do it.

348
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:14,968
We have a favour to ask.

349
00:12:15,378 --> 00:12:17,207
Do you know Wonstein?

350
00:12:17,208 --> 00:12:18,907
- He's a rapper.
- Wonstein, the rapper,

351
00:12:18,908 --> 00:12:21,248
- was featured on "Milk Shake."
- Right.

352
00:12:21,408 --> 00:12:24,048
But he can't come today.

353
00:12:24,818 --> 00:12:26,348
We need either Kwangstein...

354
00:12:27,448 --> 00:12:28,717
He released an album.

355
00:12:28,718 --> 00:12:29,894
- He's a singer.
- or Leestein.

356
00:12:29,918 --> 00:12:32,088
- Can you rap?
- What do you think?

357
00:12:32,888 --> 00:12:34,227
- You can do it.
- What?

358
00:12:34,228 --> 00:12:36,098
You're a singer.

359
00:12:36,598 --> 00:12:37,727
You released an album.

360
00:12:37,728 --> 00:12:39,127
You say I'm a singer only at a moment like this.

361
00:12:39,128 --> 00:12:40,827
Make a decision. One of you two has to do it.

362
00:12:40,828 --> 00:12:42,697
Kwang Kyu is a singer. He can do it.

363
00:12:42,698 --> 00:12:44,338
You do it.

364
00:12:44,968 --> 00:12:46,107
(I'm not confident in my rapping skills.)

365
00:12:46,108 --> 00:12:48,108
- Look at your pose.
- You two can split the rap.

366
00:12:48,338 --> 00:12:50,077
- Four bars each.
- Four bars each.

367
00:12:50,078 --> 00:12:51,977
You make a decision and let us know.

368
00:12:51,978 --> 00:12:53,907
- You can do it. You can lip-sync.
- One of you...

369
00:12:53,908 --> 00:12:55,417
Okay. I'll lip-sync then.

370
00:12:55,418 --> 00:12:56,738
(Which one will become Wonstein?)

371
00:12:57,618 --> 00:12:59,118
The weather is amazing.

372
00:12:59,388 --> 00:13:00,448
It's a beautiful day.

373
00:13:02,158 --> 00:13:05,257
Even when I work with Ye Eun,

374
00:13:05,258 --> 00:13:06,287
- we take separate cars.
- Right.

375
00:13:06,288 --> 00:13:08,327
- It's nice to ride together...
- It feels strange.

376
00:13:08,328 --> 00:13:10,398
And chat on the way.

377
00:13:11,698 --> 00:13:14,398
(Checking today's schedule)

378
00:13:14,628 --> 00:13:17,537
So it's Chungju Park Music Festival.

379
00:13:17,538 --> 00:13:18,884
It means there will be other singers too.

380
00:13:18,908 --> 00:13:19,937
Many singers will come.

381
00:13:19,938 --> 00:13:21,337
- Famous singers.
- No one knows...

382
00:13:21,338 --> 00:13:22,777
- we're going.
- Right.

383
00:13:22,778 --> 00:13:24,877
We're surprise guests.

384
00:13:24,878 --> 00:13:27,607
We're not included in the official lineup.

385
00:13:27,608 --> 00:13:28,954
(They're going to perform as surprise guests.)

386
00:13:28,978 --> 00:13:30,347
You're surprise guests.

387
00:13:30,348 --> 00:13:32,024
It means you're the highlight of the show.

388
00:13:32,048 --> 00:13:33,117
(His compliment puts a big smile on her face.)

389
00:13:33,118 --> 00:13:35,857
That's not necessarily true. I saw the lineup.

390
00:13:35,858 --> 00:13:37,388
There are so many famous singers.

391
00:13:38,218 --> 00:13:41,087
(Among a star-studded lineup of famous singers, )

392
00:13:41,088 --> 00:13:45,468
(they'll take the stage as surprise guests.)

393
00:13:45,798 --> 00:13:48,227
Do you want to listen to our song?

394
00:13:48,228 --> 00:13:50,097
- Yes, let's listen.
- Do you want to hear it?

395
00:13:50,098 --> 00:13:51,967
Play the song. It's really nice.

396
00:13:51,968 --> 00:13:53,337
The song is so...

397
00:13:53,338 --> 00:13:56,677
- Yes. In the past.
- It was written by famous people.

398
00:13:56,678 --> 00:13:58,007
("Milk Shake" by CHOONGJU JI-C)

399
00:13:58,008 --> 00:13:59,078
This is Ye Eun's voice.

400
00:14:00,178 --> 00:14:01,508
It's high.

401
00:14:02,018 --> 00:14:03,517
- It's high.
- Right?

402
00:14:03,518 --> 00:14:06,388
- Isn't her voice cute?
- She sounds so good.

403
00:14:07,588 --> 00:14:11,357
(My Dolphin Star jumps again at his compliment.)

404
00:14:11,358 --> 00:14:13,188
The song itself is very high-pitched.

405
00:14:13,658 --> 00:14:14,757
- "Milk Shake" and...
- Right.

406
00:14:14,758 --> 00:14:16,027
"AQUA" is high too.

407
00:14:16,028 --> 00:14:17,604
(The quality of the song is better than they thought.)

408
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:18,897
Vata choreographed...

409
00:14:18,898 --> 00:14:20,597
"Milk Shake."

410
00:14:20,598 --> 00:14:21,767
Right.

411
00:14:21,768 --> 00:14:22,968
He did.

412
00:14:23,398 --> 00:14:25,337
He doesn't work for anyone.

413
00:14:25,338 --> 00:14:26,707
- Right.
- So...

414
00:14:26,708 --> 00:14:29,407
Bbatta is quite famous as a choreographer, isn't he?

415
00:14:29,408 --> 00:14:31,707
He's a world-renowned choreographer.

416
00:14:31,708 --> 00:14:34,777
- He's very famous.
- World-renowned? I didn't know.

417
00:14:34,778 --> 00:14:37,417
He worked for Jennie.

418
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,647
- He did?
- Yes.

419
00:14:38,648 --> 00:14:40,748
- Jennie of BLACKPINK?
- Yes. "like JENNIE."

420
00:14:41,418 --> 00:14:42,917
(I see.)

421
00:14:42,918 --> 00:14:46,557
I think they had a crush on each other back then.

422
00:14:46,558 --> 00:14:48,257
- Is that so?
- But I didn't notice.

423
00:14:48,258 --> 00:14:49,427
Did you start dating then?

424
00:14:49,428 --> 00:14:51,627
He choreographed our song because he had feelings for me.

425
00:14:51,628 --> 00:14:52,927
That's why he did it.

426
00:14:52,928 --> 00:14:54,097
(He choreographed their song because he had a crush on her.)

427
00:14:54,098 --> 00:14:57,497
We practised for around two hours with Vata.

428
00:14:57,498 --> 00:15:00,808
It was around 9:30pm.

429
00:15:01,268 --> 00:15:04,607
I felt like I had to look after her.

430
00:15:04,608 --> 00:15:06,277
- I understand.
- You know why I felt that way.

431
00:15:06,278 --> 00:15:07,907
- I understand.
- I've never met Vata before.

432
00:15:07,908 --> 00:15:09,117
You were like her father.

433
00:15:09,118 --> 00:15:11,077
- I felt like I was her guardian.
- Right.

434
00:15:11,078 --> 00:15:12,217
Because she's my teammate,

435
00:15:12,218 --> 00:15:13,947
- and she practised because of me.
- Yes.

436
00:15:13,948 --> 00:15:16,657
She said she was fine,

437
00:15:16,658 --> 00:15:18,317
but I made sure she got in a cab and went home.

438
00:15:18,318 --> 00:15:20,087
Yes. He called a cab.

439
00:15:20,088 --> 00:15:22,657
I made sure to watch her get in the cab and go home.

440
00:15:22,658 --> 00:15:23,897
And you didn't want to go home, did you?

441
00:15:23,898 --> 00:15:26,327
- I didn't want to go.
- You didn't want to go.

442
00:15:26,328 --> 00:15:28,567
- But he wouldn't leave...
- I'm sure...

443
00:15:28,568 --> 00:15:29,967
until I got in the cab.

444
00:15:29,968 --> 00:15:31,497
- you hated it.
- I said,

445
00:15:31,498 --> 00:15:32,867
"The driver accepted."

446
00:15:32,868 --> 00:15:34,507
He said, "I'll make sure to watch you get in the cab."

447
00:15:34,508 --> 00:15:36,778
"No, the driver accepted."

448
00:15:37,078 --> 00:15:38,748
He ended up watching me get in the cab.

449
00:15:39,478 --> 00:15:41,478
So I took a cab around the block and then got out.

450
00:15:42,078 --> 00:15:44,248
- Really?
- I asked the driver to drop me off.

451
00:15:44,918 --> 00:15:47,517
(Love always comes back.)

452
00:15:47,518 --> 00:15:49,487
So you guys got together because of the song.

453
00:15:49,488 --> 00:15:51,487
It played a part.

454
00:15:51,488 --> 00:15:52,488
(The song brought them together.)

455
00:15:52,489 --> 00:15:54,927
- That's why.
- You don't have much time left.

456
00:15:54,928 --> 00:15:56,898
Our wedding is around the corner.

457
00:15:57,428 --> 00:15:58,828
It still doesn't feel real, though.

458
00:15:59,128 --> 00:16:00,297
Why don't you take your time?

459
00:16:00,298 --> 00:16:02,237
- Wait until it gets warmer.
- But I...

460
00:16:02,238 --> 00:16:04,968
love the end of the year.

461
00:16:05,138 --> 00:16:06,168
It's cold.

462
00:16:06,768 --> 00:16:08,567
Yes. Get married in the spring, when it gets warmer.

463
00:16:08,568 --> 00:16:09,978
- Right.
- It's okay. I'm young.

464
00:16:11,378 --> 00:16:13,407
- How old is he?
- We're the same age.

465
00:16:13,408 --> 00:16:15,718
- The same age.
- It's too soon.

466
00:16:16,418 --> 00:16:18,478
If you're the same age, you'll argue a lot.

467
00:16:19,188 --> 00:16:21,317
We don't really argue that much.

468
00:16:21,318 --> 00:16:22,958
It's different when you live together.

469
00:16:23,288 --> 00:16:24,288
There are some cases of married couples having...

470
00:16:24,288 --> 00:16:25,288
- arguments right after marriage.
- Right.

471
00:16:25,289 --> 00:16:27,769
You have to learn to adjust to each other when you're married.

472
00:16:28,228 --> 00:16:30,298
You have to be patient.

473
00:16:30,498 --> 00:16:33,698
But once you're married,

474
00:16:33,998 --> 00:16:37,068
there may be things you want to do but can't.

475
00:16:37,268 --> 00:16:38,437
Both of them are single,

476
00:16:38,438 --> 00:16:40,807
but they give you a lot of advice on marriage, right?

477
00:16:40,808 --> 00:16:41,908
Tell me about it.

478
00:16:43,108 --> 00:16:44,238
They know nothing about it.

479
00:16:45,948 --> 00:16:47,478
They've never gotten married.

480
00:16:50,448 --> 00:16:51,818
I bet they'll never get married.

481
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:56,257
(My Star and the secretaries are worried about each other.)

482
00:16:56,258 --> 00:16:57,318
Oh, no.

483
00:16:58,688 --> 00:17:00,958
I don't think they'll ever be able to get married.

484
00:17:02,898 --> 00:17:04,328
Especially Seo Jin.

485
00:17:06,868 --> 00:17:09,297
- Your prime is between...
- Right.

486
00:17:09,298 --> 00:17:11,368
- It's your peak.
- your mid-30s and mid-40s.

487
00:17:12,208 --> 00:17:15,237
I'm happy when I have work,

488
00:17:15,238 --> 00:17:17,638
but I don't think work is everything.

489
00:17:17,908 --> 00:17:20,407
You figured that out very early.

490
00:17:20,408 --> 00:17:22,118
I realised it when I was sick.

491
00:17:22,378 --> 00:17:24,348
She was sick before.

492
00:17:25,588 --> 00:17:26,987
She was sick. Right.

493
00:17:26,988 --> 00:17:29,517
I spent a long time unemployed,

494
00:17:29,518 --> 00:17:31,957
so I used to think I could just focus on working.

495
00:17:31,958 --> 00:17:33,927
But when I got sick,

496
00:17:33,928 --> 00:17:37,357
it made me realise that you never know how much time you have left.

497
00:17:37,358 --> 00:17:38,457
(Getting sick changed her priorities in life.)

498
00:17:38,458 --> 00:17:41,727
Well, it doesn't kill you anyway, so...

499
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:42,837
Well...

500
00:17:42,838 --> 00:17:45,238
She was so bright. But I was really worried.

501
00:17:45,468 --> 00:17:48,138
She was like, "I'm fine. I have about seven cancerous nodules."

502
00:17:48,668 --> 00:17:50,777
So are you fully recovered? Or are you still...

503
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:52,037
- undergoing treatment?
- I just have...

504
00:17:52,038 --> 00:17:54,507
- regular checkups.
- You have to be careful, though.

505
00:17:54,508 --> 00:17:58,147
Right. You have to keep checked once a year.

506
00:17:58,148 --> 00:18:00,387
People who go through a serious illness when they're young...

507
00:18:00,388 --> 00:18:02,157
end up living healthier, longer lives.

508
