1489
00:51:28,088 --> 00:51:29,657
- He's too good.
- It's Isaac Hong before you.

1490
00:51:29,658 --> 00:51:30,658
- What am I going to do?
- That's not good.

1491
00:51:30,659 --> 00:51:32,459
- His singing skill is amazing.
- That's why!

1492
00:51:32,628 --> 00:51:35,427
I'll excite the audience...

1493
00:51:35,428 --> 00:51:37,997
- Will you do that?
- with "Open Sesame."

1494
00:51:37,998 --> 00:51:39,398
Okay. That's a good idea.

1495
00:51:39,638 --> 00:51:41,537
I think that's an amazing idea.

1496
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:42,667
Otherwise...

1497
00:51:42,668 --> 00:51:45,207
He majors in music education at Berklee College of Music.

1498
00:51:45,208 --> 00:51:46,237
